> It's the same approach as having the assets from GCP PD operator repo copied here to legacy dir and testing with those right? 

@RomanBednar ,  you are right, in this PR asset yaml files in `generated` dir are exactly the same as in `legacy/...gcp.../assets`. However, the way how these assets look like runtime, on API-server, depends on custom go code we currently have in `legacy/...gcp.../starter.go`. Re-implementing this code inside csi-operator framework makes this PR non-trivial (you can see many commits in this PR on top of the first commit). The benefit of merging this PR with pre-defined assets in `generated` dir is to prove that the code really works and nothing overlooked.

The next PR auto-generating assets will have a benefit -- we can check how it works compiler-time without any cloud involved, just by comparing pre-defined assets with results of `hack/update-generated-assets.sh`. That PR may be complex, but very easy to test.

